  'soshanguve-mabopane-low-water-pressure-zuikerbosch-2026-10-12',
  'Power failure leaves Soshanguve, Mabopane with low water pressure',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-12', 'Rekord', 'https://citizen.co.za/rekord/uncategorized/2026/10/12/water-supply-disruption-hits-soshanguve-communities-following-treatment-plant-power-failure',
  'A Rand Water power failure on 9 October has left large parts of Soshanguve and Mabopane with low water pressure, the City of Tshwane says.',
  'Taps in Soshanguve and Mabopane are running at reduced pressure because of a fault at Rand Water''s Zuikerbosch plant on 9 October, the City of Tshwane says. Officials say the resulting dip in pumping capacity slowed the rate at which the Hartebeeshoek Reservoir refills, cutting the volume reaching the Soshanguve L Reservoir that feeds these suburbs.

The City''s list of areas feeling the pinch runs from Soshanguve, counting every extension, through to Soshanguve East and South. Mabopane Block S and Bon Accord AH are on the list too, and so is De Beers. Kopanong and Kopanong Ext 1 are named as well, along with Kruisfontein and Onderstepoort, then finally Rietgat, The Farm and Wentzelrust. Homes and businesses sitting on higher ground, in what officials call the Tower zone, are struggling most.

A statement attributed to municipal spokesperson Lindela Mashigo says the metro is tracking reservoir levels as the network recovers and is sorry for the disruption this has caused. No restoration date has been set, and households in those suburbs have been told to limit their water use for now. A separate DA Gauteng statement on 12 October tied the shortage to the same Zuikerbosch fault, noting it also reduced pumping at the connected Palmiet system and warning that Gauteng''s water network keeps failing in this way.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://citizen.co.za/rekord/uncategorized/2026/10/12/water-supply-disruption-hits-soshanguve-communities-following-treatment-plant-power-failure", "https://dagauteng.org.za/2026/10/one-electrical-fault-millions-at-risk-gautengs-water-infrastructure-cannot-continue-operating-on-a-knife-edge"]',
  'agent'
);
